WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.075
Step four reads the certifications
and the ServiceNow findings.

2
00:00:04.075 --> 00:00:07.036
Each account is due by its risk tier:

3
00:00:07.036 --> 00:00:12.038
R one every three months, R two
every six, R three every twelve.

4
00:00:12.038 --> 00:00:18.962
G M S A dash print is R three, last
certified in October 2025, so it's overdue.

5
00:00:18.962 --> 00:00:22.299
And its owner revoked it, so
it becomes a stale access

6
00:00:22.299 --> 00:00:25.637
finding for ServiceNow,
without anyone retyping it.

7
00:00:25.637 --> 00:00:30.562
The second finding is an orphan
account, on G M S A dash web.

8
00:00:30.562 --> 00:00:33.616
Look back at step two's
warning on the same account:

9
00:00:33.616 --> 00:00:37.712
a certification decided by someone
who isn't an owner doesn't count.

10
00:00:37.712 --> 00:00:41.710
The code writes these findings as
the payload a ServiceNow import

11
00:00:41.710 --> 00:00:45.620
or the integration kit's client
posts; it doesn't post them itself.
